ing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +1ms service=bus type=message.part.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb3687fbfffeP1kxYuj4KPTloB type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +3ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb3687fbfffeP1kxYuj4KPTloB sessionID=ses_eb3687fbfffeP1kxYuj4KPTloB unlocking\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\nI fixed six bugs in `catalog/`, but I couldn't run `python3 -m unittest` because I don't have a shell here. I checked each fix against the tests by reading them, but the suite still needs a run to confirm it passes.\n\n- **`fees.py`:** the late fee added the daily rate to the day count instead of multiplying, so it's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- **`members.py`:** the borrow limit was 3; it's now 5, which matches the comment and the tests.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns the last `n` events, or an empty list when `n <= 0`.\n- **`factory.py`:** the sample data was missing the third book, so I added `Emma` (Austen, 1815).\n- **`books.py`:** `parse_book` now stores the year as a number instead of text, which also makes `age()` work.\n- **`search.py`:** it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist; it now imports it from `catalog.text`.INFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=app name=lsp shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=app name=session shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:42 +0ms service=app name=mcp shutdown\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params